(1717127, 230155, 29556, '<td valign="top">Perfect.</td>', 'Perfect.', '2005-09-18 00:12:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1717134, 228988, 19982, '<td valign="top">I expected a lot of "looking up at the building" shots.  Some of what I''ve seen I haven''t really cared for all that much.  I really like this one though.  I think what makes it different are the many patterns within the image.  Like the almost "ladder-like steps" leading straight up the middle.  The circles with spokes at the top.  The v-shaped lines leading from the sides inward.  All of these patterns work well to bring your eyes right into the picture.  Well done!</td>', 'I expected a lot of "looking up at the building" shots.  Some of what I''ve seen I haven''t really cared for all that much.  I really like this one though.  I think what makes it different are the many patterns within the image.  Like the almost "ladder-like steps" leading straight up the middle.  The circles with spokes at the top.  The v-shaped lines leading from the sides inward.  All of these patterns work well to bring your eyes right into the picture.  Well done!', '2005-09-18 00:23:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1717138, 228659, 19982, '<td valign="top">At first I thought the picture was blurry, until I noticed the sharp focus on the end of the violin.  After noticing that, I think it was probably done on purpose and I would congratulate you on the DOF.  But...  for my own personal taste, I just don''t agree with the idea.  I would be far more interested in seeing the girls eyes in focus (and not covered by the bow) and then allow the violin to move out of focus due to DOF.  I give you points for your creative use of DOF.  Just not as much as if I agreed more with the application.  Hope that makes sense.</td>', 'At first I thought the picture was blurry, until I noticed the sharp focus on the end of the violin.  After noticing that, I think it was probably done on purpose and I would congratulate you on the DOF.  But...  for my own personal taste, I just don''t agree with the idea.  I would be far more interested in seeing the girls eyes in focus (and not covered by the bow) and then allow the violin to move out of focus due to DOF.  I give you points for your creative use of DOF.  Just not as much as if I agreed more with the application.  Hope that makes sense.', '2005-09-18 00:28:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1717143, 231158, 43329, '<td valign="top">Sorry, I''m not fussy about the inverting of the colours to give the effect of a negative view... it doesn''t enhance the idea of perspective for me.</td>', 'Sorry, I''m not fussy about the inverting of the colours to give the effect of a negative view... it doesn''t enhance the idea of perspective for me.', '2005-09-18 00:31:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1717148, 230986, 43329, '<td valign="top">Sorry, the odd colours detracted from the low-angle point of view, and they don''t enhance the idea of perspective for me.</td>', 'Sorry, the odd colours detracted from the low-angle point of view, and they don''t enhance the idea of perspective for me.', '2005-09-18 00:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1717157, 230761, 43329, '<td valign="top">What a great idea for a portrait! Too bad that the image is so badly artifacted... I would love to see this gentleman''s character presented more clearly.</td>', 'What a great idea for a portrait! Too bad that the image is so badly artifacted... I would love to see this gentleman''s character presented more clearly.', '2005-09-18 00:36:59.000000', NULL, 1),
