(1726489, 230627, 40819, '<td valign="top">Hello and thanks for the great votes and remarks. <br/> <br/>I thought I would explain something to all of you, I was out on September 10th taking some really cool shots of speed boats at Liberty State Park in NJ for the perspective challenge, the location I was at was directly across the Hudson River from where the WTC once stood. This always gives me pause and a chance to reflect on things I have done and things I might have done in my life for many reasons. So I just couldn''t let my desire to score high in a photo challenge overcome my desire to pay tribute to my personal loss on 9/11. This is why I shot the lights and didn''t enter all those cool shots of the boats. <br/> <br/>If you would like to read a personal story of my 9/11 you can go to <a href="//magicalmike.com/html/fr__mychal_judge.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//magicalmike.com/html/fr__mychal_judge.html</a> <br/>To watch a flash tribute to the people of NYC (which I made though only one of the images is mine the first one) go here: <br/><a href="//magicalmike.com/html/never_forget_9_11_2001.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//magicalmike.com/html/never_forget_9_11_2001.html</a> <br/> <br/>So look at that, I followed my heart and ended up with the highest rated entry to DP Challenge so far. Thank you all for your votes and noticing. <br/> <br/>BTW if you look closely, I wasn''t the only one who had this idea. I counted at least 3 other views of the Tribute in light. Good job all. For those not from around here, this is a one night light show which commemorates the loss we all sustained on 9/11. It can be seen over 20 miles away. The lights were placed in a different spot this year about 1/4 mile south of where the Twin Towers originally stood. <br/> <br/>From the angle I took this shot the towers would have fallen right in front of the Statue of Liberty not so far to the right. <br/> <br/>Be well all and thank you again for the votes and comments. <br/> <br/>Michael<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-09-21 12:21:16.</i></td>', 'Hello and thanks for the great votes and remarks.  I thought I would explain something to all of you, I was out on September 10th taking some really cool shots of speed boats at Liberty State Park in NJ for the perspective challenge, the location I was at was directly across the Hudson River from where the WTC once stood. This always gives me pause and a chance to reflect on things I have done and things I might have done in my life for many reasons. So I just couldn''t let my desire to score high in a photo challenge overcome my desire to pay tribute to my personal loss on 9/11. This is why I shot the lights and didn''t enter all those cool shots of the boats.  If you would like to read a personal story of my 9/11 you can go to //magicalmike.com/html/fr__mychal_judge.html To watch a flash tribute to the people of NYC (which I made though only one of the images is mine the first one) go here: //magicalmike.com/html/never_forget_9_11_2001.html  So look at that, I followed my heart and ended up with the highest rated entry to DP Challenge so far. Thank you all for your votes and noticing.  BTW if you look closely, I wasn''t the only one who had this idea. I counted at least 3 other views of the Tribute in light. Good job all. For those not from around here, this is a one night light show which commemorates the loss we all sustained on 9/11. It can be seen over 20 miles away. The lights were placed in a different spot this year about 1/4 mile south of where the Twin Towers originally stood.  From the angle I took this shot the towers would have fallen right in front of the Statue of Liberty not so far to the right.  Be well all and thank you again for the votes and comments.  Michael', '2005-09-21 09:37:21.000000', '2005-09-21 13:21:16.000000', 0),
(1726500, 229348, 41673, '<td valign="top">I like it more every time I look at it. It was in my top 3! Beautiful color composition.</td>', 'I like it more every time I look at it. It was in my top 3! Beautiful color composition.', '2005-09-21 09:41:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1726509, 229364, 41673, '<td valign="top">Had you much higher. I love the simplicity and composition.</td>', 'Had you much higher. I love the simplicity and composition.', '2005-09-21 09:45:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(1726526, 231352, 42574, '<td valign="top">I really appreciate the comments - particularly regarding the lighting (good or bad), as this was tough for me to get. I wasn''t entirely happy with the look, but I thought it was the best of a number of takes. If someone has more suggestions on how to improve this, I would love to hear them. I make knives (this is one of mine!), and photographing a blade with a mirror finish has always given me some trouble.<br/> <br/>For this shot, I lit the subject from the left side and held one larger &amp; one smaller piece of white card as reflectors in key positions to diffuse a little light &amp; control glare. But, as some rightly noted, I somewhat lost the reflective appearance of the shiny blade.</td>', 'I really appreciate the comments - particularly regarding the lighting (good or bad), as this was tough for me to get. I wasn''t entirely happy with the look, but I thought it was the best of a number of takes. If someone has more suggestions on how to improve this, I would love to hear them. I make knives (this is one of mine!), and photographing a blade with a mirror finish has always given me some trouble. For this shot, I lit the subject from the left side and held one larger & one smaller piece of white card as reflectors in key positions to diffuse a little light & control glare. But, as some rightly noted, I somewhat lost the reflective appearance of the shiny blade.', '2005-09-21 09:53:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1726537, 230892, 41673, '<td valign="top">Third one in the out takes would have been awesome!</td>', 'Third one in the out takes would have been awesome!', '2005-09-21 09:56:59.000000', NULL, 0),
