(1730335, 230822, 42139, '<td valign="top">It was ment to be simple though, I guess it''s because I''m from a design background (Photography being a hobby) It wasn''t supposed to be over powering, because when I look up at the sky in they city it seems like the only peaceful place down town.</td>', 'It was ment to be simple though, I guess it''s because I''m from a design background (Photography being a hobby) It wasn''t supposed to be over powering, because when I look up at the sky in they city it seems like the only peaceful place down town.', '2005-09-22 10:26:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1730361, 229793, 42139, '<td valign="top">Alright let me say something, I wasn''t in the best mood when I posted the last one... and I didn''t even really understand what I was saying.<br/> <br/>Look the problems I see with this  picture is that the naked woman distracts the picture too much, I think I understand the message you were trying to put across... but I saw this concept several times before I got to your picture, and the images before always set the tone for the rest. <br/> <br/>As for me saying "The prespective is stupid" What I should have side is that it''s not strong... It would be much better if you had put the show to the left, so that you went from the shoe to the naked woman.. then she would seem more like part of the image, then and after thoguht.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Alright let me say something, I wasn''t in the best mood when I posted the last one... and I didn''t even really understand what I was saying. Look the problems I see with this  picture is that the naked woman distracts the picture too much, I think I understand the message you were trying to put across... but I saw this concept several times before I got to your picture, and the images before always set the tone for the rest.  As for me saying "The prespective is stupid" What I should have side is that it''s not strong... It would be much better if you had put the show to the left, so that you went from the shoe to the naked woman.. then she would seem more like part of the image, then and after thoguht. ', '2005-09-22 10:43:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1730368, 228881, 39349, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, I like the b/w. I didn''t make it to this shot during voting but I would suspect I would have given it in the 4-5-6 range. Lighting is interesting and the angle works. Blur on the right hand side is a bit distracting and takes away from this shot IMHO, tighter crop and or adjusting DOF would make this better.<br/></td>', 'Nice shot, I like the b/w. I didn''t make it to this shot during voting but I would suspect I would have given it in the 4-5-6 range. Lighting is interesting and the angle works. Blur on the right hand side is a bit distracting and takes away from this shot IMHO, tighter crop and or adjusting DOF would make this better.', '2005-09-22 10:47:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1730568, 230390, 22379, '<td valign="top">I cant believe someone wanted the train in the picture! You dont have to listen for the train when you can SEE it!!!<br/>I admit the thumb looked a bit morbid, but the full view you see the hobo stick and it is more that apparent that hes a runaway looking to catch a ride. <br/>I think its a great storyboard.</td>', 'I cant believe someone wanted the train in the picture! You dont have to listen for the train when you can SEE it!!!I admit the thumb looked a bit morbid, but the full view you see the hobo stick and it is more that apparent that hes a runaway looking to catch a ride. I think its a great storyboard.', '2005-09-22 12:42:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1730624, 228954, 38592, '<td valign="top">Wow... this is an AMAZING capture of beavertail.  The colors and use of long exposure to smooth the water really look great in this picture.  I work not far from here so I am going to have to try and get a few picture of it also.  Good to see another RI photographer on here!</td>', 'Wow... this is an AMAZING capture of beavertail.  The colors and use of long exposure to smooth the water really look great in this picture.  I work not far from here so I am going to have to try and get a few picture of it also.  Good to see another RI photographer on here!', '2005-09-22 13:08:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1730718, 229946, 42871, '<td valign="top">I admit I was a little blocked when it came to what I was going to shoot. Originally I was going to do something with the Jefferson memorial, with its nice curve of columns it makes a nice subject. Of course when I saw that it also won the previous Perspectives challenge it kind of threw a wrench into my plan. After looking through the almost 100 pictures I had taken for this, I just kept coming back to this one. I cropped to the top of the monument, which was basically flat at that point anyway, to kind of make it appear like a road up into the sky. Had I to do it all over again I think I would have shot it at the corner to add some depth to the image. As it is, there is just not enough texture to the top half of the image.</td>', 'I admit I was a little blocked when it came to what I was going to shoot. Originally I was going to do something with the Jefferson memorial, with its nice curve of columns it makes a nice subject. Of course when I saw that it also won the previous Perspectives challenge it kind of threw a wrench into my plan. After looking through the almost 100 pictures I had taken for this, I just kept coming back to this one. I cropped to the top of the monument, which was basically flat at that point anyway, to kind of make it appear like a road up into the sky. Had I to do it all over again I think I would have shot it at the corner to add some depth to the image. As it is, there is just not enough texture to the top half of the image.', '2005-09-22 13:42:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1730743, 228883, 28710, '<td valign="top">I think I got it.<br/> <br/>Is it the view from the Phantom of the Opera on a Rose that he wishes he could give to Christine? Obsession. Gotcha.<br/> <br/>WOO. Do I get a Prize if that''s it?<br/> <br/>Speech? Uhm, I''d like to thank the Academy and oh, yeah, Sherri1209 for helping a bit with the concept.<br/> <br/>You got your focal point right. The rose looks crisp. I wonder if you could have had more view of the subject though. This would likely have involved moving closer to the mask. Looks to me like that would have made it more difficult to get as much of the mask in and have people recognize the mask, but perhaps it would be worth it for more of the rose?</td>', 'I think I got it. Is it the view from the Phantom of the Opera on a Rose that he wishes he could give to Christine? Obsession. Gotcha. WOO. Do I get a Prize if that''s it? Speech? Uhm, I''d like to thank the Academy and oh, yeah, Sherri1209 for helping a bit with the concept. You got your focal point right. The rose looks crisp. I wonder if you could have had more view of the subject though. This would likely have involved moving closer to the mask. Looks to me like that would have made it more difficult to get as much of the mask in and have people recognize the mask, but perhaps it would be worth it for more of the rose?', '2005-09-22 13:48:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1730832, 230847, 40370, '<td valign="top">I didn''t have a chance to vote on the perspective challenge, once again your entry has done very well, congratulations. I love the crop of the lions ... corner to corner. Go SLC !</td>', 'I didn''t have a chance to vote on the perspective challenge, once again your entry has done very well, congratulations. I love the crop of the lions ... corner to corner. Go SLC !', '2005-09-22 14:20:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1731060, 231035, 30049, '<td valign="top">Nice shot Skip.  Noisy at the office - eh?  ;^)  I like how there is a natural line formed from the front of the car, thru the pit crew guys on the track, up to the Goodwrench flag in the corner.  The track lighting brings in a parallel line from the top.  I''m not really sure what type of perspective you were going for here but I like it anyway.  He-he.</td>', 'Nice shot Skip.  Noisy at the office - eh?  ;^)  I like how there is a natural line formed from the front of the car, thru the pit crew guys on the track, up to the Goodwrench flag in the corner.  The track lighting brings in a parallel line from the top.  I''m not really sure what type of perspective you were going for here but I like it anyway.  He-he.', '2005-09-22 16:29:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1731066, 231095, 30049, '<td valign="top">Those darn power lines get in the way!  JK.  ;^)  This shot does a good job of taking the viewer thru the image.  I like the color treatment on the sky.  You''re brave to take on this type of subject...it''s hard to avoid jaggies on resize to 640 with all the lines.<br/> <br/>Smile and keep having fun!</td>', 'Those darn power lines get in the way!  JK.  ;^)  This shot does a good job of taking the viewer thru the image.  I like the color treatment on the sky.  You''re brave to take on this type of subject...it''s hard to avoid jaggies on resize to 640 with all the lines. Smile and keep having fun!', '2005-09-22 16:35:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1731169, 229793, 39088, '<td valign="top">Thank you Silience, that is helpfull.</td>', 'Thank you Silience, that is helpfull.', '2005-09-22 17:22:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1731197, 230245, 14614, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get to vote on 100% of this challenge so no "actual" score.  I would have scored it on the high side for a few reasons:<br/>- placement of the main element is great (central and yet not symetrical)<br/>- it''s an interesting tone and the muted colors give it a woody, hushed feel<br/>- post processing shows care and an artistic touch<br/> <br/>Only (very small) negative, the clump in the center detracts from the simple lines.<br/> <br/>Theresa</td>', 'I didn''t get to vote on 100% of this challenge so no "actual" score.  I would have scored it on the high side for a few reasons:- placement of the main element is great (central and yet not symetrical)- it''s an interesting tone and the muted colors give it a woody, hushed feel- post processing shows care and an artistic touch Only (very small) negative, the clump in the center detracts from the simple lines. Theresa', '2005-09-22 17:35:30.000000', NULL, 0),
