(1757946, 230658, 11738, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by graphicfunk:</b></div><hr/><i> This great image is missing only a ribbon. By far, my favorite of the challenge and an outstanding b/w study. Congratulations on your top 20 finish. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This message, especially coming from Daniel, means the world to me.  To be appreciated by someone with so much talent and experience makes me realize that I may have some photographic talent after all.  A real confidence booster.<br/> <br/>Thanks again Daniel.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-10-04 11:29:34.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by graphicfunk: This great image is missing only a ribbon. By far, my favorite of the challenge and an outstanding b/w study. Congratulations on your top 20 finish.   This message, especially coming from Daniel, means the world to me.  To be appreciated by someone with so much talent and experience makes me realize that I may have some photographic talent after all.  A real confidence booster. Thanks again Daniel.', '2005-10-04 11:59:31.000000', '2005-10-04 12:29:34.000000', 0),
(1760534, 230541, 38032, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for the comments and good scores.  To answer questions:  I could have only removed the debris manually (before the photo). Also: The title means: "The Man in the Floor".  I thought this was better not to be blatantly titled since there were a few things to focus on and discover.</td>', 'Thanks everyone for the comments and good scores.  To answer questions:  I could have only removed the debris manually (before the photo). Also: The title means: "The Man in the Floor".  I thought this was better not to be blatantly titled since there were a few things to focus on and discover.', '2005-10-05 08:24:04.000000', NULL, 0),
