(1783964, 230995, 32997, '<td valign="top">I don''t think your image is grainy..your focus on the dog is not sharp though. This is an interesting perspective..I find it too busy (and I often like busy)..the shed doesn''t add to this subject..there is nothing gained from my pov in seeing it..the grass being in the foreground is distracting because it is not in focus and is not the subject..if the grass is tha tprominent I would think it might be better to give it the sharp focus, and have the dog out of focus..if the dog is the focal pt. then the grass would work better if it framed him. As for the not sharp focus,  think it would have helped to bump up your iso, and use a faster shutter speed to accomadate the dog''s movement (i am constantly guilty of using too slow a shutter speed myself).<br/>Of course you might see things completely differently..that is a given. Hope this helps.</td>', 'I don''t think your image is grainy..your focus on the dog is not sharp though. This is an interesting perspective..I find it too busy (and I often like busy)..the shed doesn''t add to this subject..there is nothing gained from my pov in seeing it..the grass being in the foreground is distracting because it is not in focus and is not the subject..if the grass is tha tprominent I would think it might be better to give it the sharp focus, and have the dog out of focus..if the dog is the focal pt. then the grass would work better if it framed him. As for the not sharp focus,  think it would have helped to bump up your iso, and use a faster shutter speed to accomadate the dog''s movement (i am constantly guilty of using too slow a shutter speed myself).Of course you might see things completely differently..that is a given. Hope this helps.', '2005-10-14 12:46:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1787425, 229120, 45965, '<td valign="top">Superb use of distortion and perspective, love it!<br/>Black and white is a good choice too.</td>', 'Superb use of distortion and perspective, love it!Black and white is a good choice too.', '2005-10-16 12:01:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1788047, 229870, 34659, '<td valign="top">Must admit I scored this a 5.  I really like the centered composition and the lines, but the blown out sky and color tones were distractions.  Still, a good entry - just not all I think it might have been.<br/> <br/>EDIT:  Looking forward to seeing more of your work!  Post some more pix!  :-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-10-16 16:50:13.</i></td>', 'Must admit I scored this a 5.  I really like the centered composition and the lines, but the blown out sky and color tones were distractions.  Still, a good entry - just not all I think it might have been. EDIT:  Looking forward to seeing more of your work!  Post some more pix!  :-)', '2005-10-16 17:49:39.000000', '2005-10-16 17:50:13.000000', 0),
(1788852, 231081, 29753, '<td valign="top">how did this score so low, i just love it. The color tone is great</td>', 'how did this score so low, i just love it. The color tone is great', '2005-10-17 00:12:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1791693, 231120, 34247, '<td valign="top">This shot has a potential for that "wow" factor. I think it''s simply missing a bit of contrast values. The composition is very nice, the story is there, and the artistic value is definitely also present. Bump the contrast up, I say...</td>', 'This shot has a potential for that "wow" factor. I think it''s simply missing a bit of contrast values. The composition is very nice, the story is there, and the artistic value is definitely also present. Bump the contrast up, I say...', '2005-10-18 01:41:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(1793748, 231351, 20530, '<td valign="top">Wow...incredible image. The sky is so dramatic, it reminds me of a JMW Turner painting. As I mentioned in the IM, I love the double entendre. Congratulations on your highest score, so far.</td>', 'Wow...incredible image. The sky is so dramatic, it reminds me of a JMW Turner painting. As I mentioned in the IM, I love the double entendre. Congratulations on your highest score, so far.', '2005-10-18 21:57:35.000000', NULL, 0),
