(2310866, 229732, 42025, '<td valign="top">Ahh I know this bench, right on the former great Bartlet square</td>', 'Ahh I know this bench, right on the former great Bartlet square', '2006-04-13 20:25:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2349339, 230541, 29753, '<td valign="top">amazing!!</td>', 'amazing!!', '2006-04-27 01:25:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2356071, 231351, 27845, '<td valign="top">This truly is an impressive capture, to say the least. The vastenss of the sky is incredible. The perspective suggests that the people buried here went straight "up" to heaven, into that magnificient relam of patterns and shapes, which you revealed in your excellent B&amp;W conversion. I also like how you managed to use the elements present to create a kind of natural vignette around the scene, framing the elements and keeping the composition together.</td>', 'This truly is an impressive capture, to say the least. The vastenss of the sky is incredible. The perspective suggests that the people buried here went straight "up" to heaven, into that magnificient relam of patterns and shapes, which you revealed in your excellent B&W conversion. I also like how you managed to use the elements present to create a kind of natural vignette around the scene, framing the elements and keeping the composition together.', '2006-04-29 07:29:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2360320, 228900, 47117, '<td valign="top">I love buildings taken at this angle. Nice work!</td>', 'I love buildings taken at this angle. Nice work!', '2006-04-30 00:27:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2367178, 231351, 49667, '<td valign="top">Hi, I chose this photo as it appears to be your best, at least on this site.  <br/> <br/>First, I would have scored this as a 4.  Why? there is too much contrast in this photo which leaves a lot of detail to be desired.  Granted, the subject, according to the title, was the rays of light coming in from above so perhaps you have turned the contrast up for a reason. There is a significant amount of noise in the sky to the left and I can see what appears to be speckles of dust on your sensor in the upper right to reduce the chance of this, I would have used a larger aperature--using a larger aperature would not have hurt you exposure wise if you compensated with a faster shutter speed...  I usually try not to go over F/16 on the 20D  These are the technical impurities of this photo.<br/> <br/>Now, composition wise...  looking past the technical imperfections...  Usually a photo with a border sends up a red flag that something is so wrong with the photo that it can''t stand on it''s own without a border.  Granted, borders are nice and they add to the photo when creatively used, but that''s just it... it adds to the photo, which takes away from the subject of the photo in question.  The composition is really striking... when I see this photo the thought of resurrection comes to mind; as if the rays of light are heaven opening it''s doors.  The tree in the foreground and to the right is a bit distracting which draws away from the mood you have created here.  Had you either zoomed in, or cropped the tree, or moved to your left about 15ft, then I think you would have made a better composition.</td>', 'Hi, I chose this photo as it appears to be your best, at least on this site.   First, I would have scored this as a 4.  Why? there is too much contrast in this photo which leaves a lot of detail to be desired.  Granted, the subject, according to the title, was the rays of light coming in from above so perhaps you have turned the contrast up for a reason. There is a significant amount of noise in the sky to the left and I can see what appears to be speckles of dust on your sensor in the upper right to reduce the chance of this, I would have used a larger aperature--using a larger aperature would not have hurt you exposure wise if you compensated with a faster shutter speed...  I usually try not to go over F/16 on the 20D  These are the technical impurities of this photo. Now, composition wise...  looking past the technical imperfections...  Usually a photo with a border sends up a red flag that something is so wrong with the photo that it can''t stand on it''s own without a border.  Granted, borders are nice and they add to the photo when creatively used, but that''s just it... it adds to the photo, which takes away from the subject of the photo in question.  The composition is really striking... when I see this photo the thought of resurrection comes to mind; as if the rays of light are heaven opening it''s doors.  The tree in the foreground and to the right is a bit distracting which draws away from the mood you have created here.  Had you either zoomed in, or cropped the tree, or moved to your left about 15ft, then I think you would have made a better composition.', '2006-05-01 04:41:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2367185, 231351, 47294, '<td valign="top">Well mate I think it''s a damn fine photo.</td>', 'Well mate I think it''s a damn fine photo.', '2006-05-01 04:47:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2367222, 231351, 43405, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GIS_boy:</b></div><hr/><i> Well mate I think it''s a damn fine photo. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ditto</td>', 'Originally posted by GIS_boy: Well mate I think it''s a damn fine photo.   Ditto', '2006-05-01 05:15:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2413716, 229500, 36628, '<td valign="top">I like everything about this except the tilt. Just my personal taste, its a little bit too extreme for me. I''d be interested to see a similar shot without the exaggerated angle.</td>', 'I like everything about this except the tilt. Just my personal taste, its a little bit too extreme for me. I''d be interested to see a similar shot without the exaggerated angle.', '2006-05-14 04:21:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2438037, 230717, 26513, '<td valign="top">haha this is awesome! nice one</td>', 'haha this is awesome! nice one', '2006-05-19 21:47:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2513458, 230980, 3569, '<td valign="top">Hi Bianca,<br/> <br/>Returning the comment.<br/> <br/>I went through your challenges since you have no portfolio at this time.<br/> <br/>I really like this shot and it should have done much better. <br/> <br/>My thought on the shot.  The red bike is great, it adds alot to the shot.  I believe the downfall is the angle.  If you would have shot it at a lower angle as suggested in other comments, the lines would have led the viewers eye back to the bike much better or which you probably could not do, would have been to shoot farther back to have less bike and more lines leading to the bike.  The green really complements the red and the other colors are good because they do not draw a viewers eye away from the subject bike.<br/> <br/>Overall, you were robbed, but I haven''t figured DPCers since being active.<br/> <br/> Enter more and have fun.  Best wishes,<br/> <br/>Van</td>', 'Hi Bianca, Returning the comment. I went through your challenges since you have no portfolio at this time. I really like this shot and it should have done much better.  My thought on the shot.  The red bike is great, it adds alot to the shot.  I believe the downfall is the angle.  If you would have shot it at a lower angle as suggested in other comments, the lines would have led the viewers eye back to the bike much better or which you probably could not do, would have been to shoot farther back to have less bike and more lines leading to the bike.  The green really complements the red and the other colors are good because they do not draw a viewers eye away from the subject bike. Overall, you were robbed, but I haven''t figured DPCers since being active.  Enter more and have fun.  Best wishes, Van', '2006-06-13 17:33:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2516587, 230916, 46314, '<td valign="top">Reminds me of the post boxes I used to use growing up...</td>', 'Reminds me of the post boxes I used to use growing up...', '2006-06-14 13:04:05.000000', NULL, 0),
